  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_020: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → acc 0.725), the most critical uncertainty is whether the RNA modality actually contributes meaningful signal over the image alone. Config_004 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer) is a direct ablation that holds the image encoder, aggregation, and profile setting constant while removing RNA. If image-only accuracy is close to 0.725, the multimodal fusion adds little and I should pivot budget toward optimizing the unimodal path; if it is substantially lower, multimodal fusion is confirmed as valuable and I can exploit that by tuning RNA encoder, fusion, and aggregation in subsequent runs. This single comparison resolves the highest-level design question and maximally informs the allocation of the remaining 8 experiments."
}

